  "title": "Gulbadan Begum",
  "summary": "Daughter of the first Mughal emperor Babur and half-sister of Humayun, she was born about 1522-23 and joined her father in Agra in 1527-28. Akbar directed her to write the Humayun-nama, probably begun in 1586-87; the only known copy is incomplete. In 1575-76 she went on pilgrimage to Mecca, stayed in the Hijaz three and a half years, was shipwrecked near Aden and reached India in 1582. She died in 1603.",
